Cell["\<\
Figure 13. Classical and tropical algebra side by side.  Every axiom of a \
commutative ring carries over EXCEPT additive inverses.\
\>", "Text",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Helvetica",
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,ExpressionUUID->"48d65e88-900e-4e58-adeb-25e50b301dfd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Operators in WL.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 StyleBox["\\[CirclePlus]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  Background->GrayLevel[0.95]],
 " enters via Esc+c+p+Esc and binds at low precedence; ",
 StyleBox["\\[CircleTimes]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  Background->GrayLevel[0.95]],
 " (Esc+c+t+Esc) and ",
 StyleBox["\\[CircleDot]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  Background->GrayLevel[0.95]],
 " (Esc+c+.+Esc) are similar. We define them once and never again think about \
it."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"94fa9ad1-4ae2-40af-b5cd-9f49cc5d73cb"],

Cell["\<\
(* The four max-plus operators, attached to the System` symbols so the
   infix syntax  a \\[CirclePlus] b \\[CirclePlus] c, A \\[CircleDot] B  \
works directly. *)

Unprotect[System`CirclePlus, System`CircleTimes,
           System`CircleMinus, System`CircleDot];

System`CirclePlus[a_, b_] := Max[a, b];
System`CirclePlus[a_, b__] := Max[a, b];
SetAttributes[System`CirclePlus, {Listable, Flat, OneIdentity, Orderless}];

System`CircleTimes[a_, b_] := a + b;
System`CircleTimes[a_, b__] := Plus[a, b];
SetAttributes[System`CircleTimes, {Listable, Flat, OneIdentity, Orderless}];

System`CircleDot[A_?MatrixQ, B_?MatrixQ] := Inner[Plus, A, B, Max];
System`CircleDot[A_?MatrixQ, v_?VectorQ] := Inner[Plus, A, v, Max];
System`CircleDot[v_?VectorQ, A_?MatrixQ] := Inner[Plus, v, A, Max];

Protect[System`CirclePlus, System`CircleTimes,
         System`CircleMinus, System`CircleDot];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f93f1781-4b77-433f-a060-7cc7cea383b6"],

Cell["\<\
(* try them *)
{3 \\[CirclePlus] 7, 3 \\[CircleTimes] 7, {1, 2, 3} \\[CirclePlus] {4, 0, 5}}\
\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"5d905816-602c-4365-856f-aeb6aeee6d7c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 $CellContext`text["Output:  ", 
  StyleBox[
  "{7, 10, {4, 2, 5}}", FontFamily -> "Source Code Pro", Background -> 
   GrayLevel[0.95]]]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"241a126d-a871-41d9-bfda-\
69de3aebed11"],

Cell["2.  Tropical matrices, identity, Kleene star", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"9d11db85-9141-49dd-bbe4-3f0dd29634fb"],

Cell["\<\
A tropical matrix is just a real matrix; what changes is the multiplication. \
The identity has 0 on the diagonal and -Infinity everywhere else (because \
-Infinity is the new \"zero\").\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b4c3b365-ae8a-45f2-b298-0f2f01a0a28f"],

Cell["\<\
MPIdentity[n_Integer] :=
  Normal @ SparseArray[{i_, i_} -> 0, {n, n}, -Infinity];

MPMatrixPower[A_, 0] := MPIdentity[Length[A]];
MPMatrixPower[A_, 1] := A;
MPMatrixPower[A_, k_] := Nest[A \\[CircleDot] # &, A, k - 1];

KleeneStar[A_?MatrixQ] := Module[{n = Length[A], acc, term},
  acc  = MPIdentity[n];
  term = MPIdentity[n];
  Do[
    term = A \\[CircleDot] term;
    acc  = MapThread[Max, {acc, term}, 2],
    {n - 1}];
  acc
];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"7bf14e3d-d3a5-45cb-944f-20baecab93d2"],

Cell["\<\
The Kleene star of A is the matrix whose (i, j) entry is the longest-path \
weight from i to j over paths of any length up to n - 1. On a finite directed \
graph with no positive-weight cycles this stabilises.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"00ebc964-fb86-4dc9-92ca-fd84987872a1"],

Cell["3.  Classical application 1 - shortest paths", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a7cf71b6-7448-4699-bba1-fec8b4c52e2c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 $CellContext`text["The Bellman-Ford recurrence ", 
  StyleBox[
  "d_{t+1}(v) = min_u (d_t(u) + cost(u,v))", FontFamily -> "Source Code Pro", 
   Background -> GrayLevel[0.95]], 
  " is, in min-plus algebra, literally a matrix-vector product. So the Kleene \
star on the cost matrix (negated, to flip Max to Min) gives the full \
all-pairs distance matrix in one shot."]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ce12349b-\
7d97-4b06-9994-239b944a5742"],

