Cell["\<\
Figure 5. A univariate tropical polynomial with 4 monomials and its Newton \
polygon. All four monomials sit on the upper hull, so the polynomial has 3 \
corners.\
\>", "Text",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Helvetica",
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,ExpressionUUID->"a1fdd73f-1be8-483c-975e-a3bb96d7bdac"],

Cell["\<\
The crucial fact: only monomials whose lifted point (a_i, c_i) sits on the \
UPPER convex hull contribute a non-empty region to the piecewise-linear \
envelope. Interior monomials are dominated everywhere.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4dd5dbcd-31fe-4ec5-b782-c970d574f9df"],

