Cell["\<\
Figure 14. ReLU(x) = max(0, x) is, in tropical notation, 0 \[CirclePlus] x: \
the tropical sum of the input with the multiplicative identity 0. A single \
ReLU unit is a degree-1 tropical polynomial.\
\>", "Text",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Helvetica",
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,ExpressionUUID->"a46de035-c162-485a-9b2e-b8cc29885271"],

Cell["8.  The decisive identity", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"05b6a66b-910e-4689-96d9-11db1ffa1562"],

Cell["\<\
A 1-hidden-layer ReLU classifier is a CLASSICAL SUM of ReLU units. The \
identity that lets us turn that classical sum into a single tropical \
polynomial is\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d10f6748-75b0-4b81-811b-52c3b2948060"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "  ",
 StyleBox["Max[0, A] + Max[0, B]  ==  Max[0, A, B, A + B]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  Background->GrayLevel[0.95]]
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"83d45396-3ade-4f70-b2bf-328da1577ec0"],

Cell["\<\
which, read tropically, says that the classical sum of two ReLU units is the \
tropical PRODUCT of their tropical polynomials -- each unit contributing two \
monomials, the product giving four.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"95b7a2dc-67f2-4469-872b-80b9783d54f6"],

