Cell["\<\
Figure 10. A 1-hidden-unit ReLU network rewritten as P(x1, x2) - Q(x1, x2), \
case-analysed on the sign of the output weight. The decision boundary {f = 0} \
is the tropical hypersurface {P = Q}.\
\>", "Text",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Helvetica",
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,ExpressionUUID->"81e81f3b-4fc2-431f-bb43-035c30485d84"],

Cell["10.  Two units: a proper tropical rational", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0e0176c3-e210-4761-9664-5df5627e4e22"],

Cell["\<\
With two hidden units we can already produce a non-trivial tropical rational \
map (when one output weight is negative) or a tropical polynomial with FOUR \
monomials (when both output weights are positive). The 4 monomials come from \
the identity in Section 8.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5d45b1e7-4bf9-436f-ae62-aa624cb530a0"],

