Cell["\<\
Figure 2. Decision boundary = tropical hypersurface for the three trained \
classifiers. The pastel patches are the activation-pattern regions, the thin \
grey lines are the ReLU creases, the black is the classical {f = 0} boundary, \
the red dashed is the max-plus {P = Q} hypersurface (overlaid on top -- they \
coincide).\
\>", "Text",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Helvetica",
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,ExpressionUUID->"232ed4c1-96e9-489d-a917-9e1393bf0468"],

Cell["14.  Newton polytope of the trained network", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"48358cba-78fb-45d3-a6fe-1feddf836d95"],

Cell["\<\
The tropical polynomial P (and similarly Q) for the trained moons network has \
its own Newton polytope and upper hull. The duality of Section 5 means that \
interior lifted points contribute nothing -- they are dominated everywhere.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5fa7efa0-e0e6-4e81-b303-b1b3b5452e0d"],

