Cell["\<\
Figure 3. Newton polytope of P (top row) and Q (bottom row) for the trained \
moons classifier. The 3D upper hull (left) and the linear-piece partition of \
input space (right) are dual; 4 of P's 7 monomials and 5 of Q's 7 monomials \
realise a region.\
\>", "Text",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Helvetica",
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,ExpressionUUID->"7e7cf54e-93bd-43b2-9370-d128a32847b2"],

Cell["15.  Linear regions scale like n^2", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"6c2690ad-52e8-4da7-8076-ee372de9443c"],

Cell["\<\
By Zaslavsky's theorem, n straight lines in general position in R^2 partition \
the plane into at most Z(n) = 1 + n + C(n, 2) regions. That is the \
Zhang-Naitzat-Lim upper bound for a 2-hidden-1 ReLU classifier. We sweep \
hidden width n in {2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 96} on moons (3 seeds each), count \
realised activation patterns on a fine grid, and compare.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"afcfbfe8-6c07-41a8-a178-360ab0c6f596"],

