Cell["\<\
Figure 4. Empirical linear regions vs hidden width n: the empirical curve \
tracks the Zaslavsky bound at slope 2 on log-log axes. Trained networks \
realise 0.5-0.95 of the maximum.\
\>", "Text",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Helvetica",
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,ExpressionUUID->"6682c4c5-d07a-4759-9bea-163cf36cf39b"],

Cell["16.  Putting it together", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"53b7a09b-06d1-42fd-81d1-2479368a9af2"],

Cell["The takeaway in one table:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"99f552aa-b7f9-4589-bd83-7562e843a76e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["+----------------------------------+-------------------------------\
--------+\n",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  Background->GrayLevel[0.95]],
 StyleBox["| classical / ReLU                 | tropical / max-plus           \
        |\n",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  Background->GrayLevel[0.95]],
 StyleBox["+----------------------------------+-------------------------------\
--------+\n",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  Background->GrayLevel[0.95]],
 StyleBox["| max(0, W x + b) per layer        | tropical polynomial in x      \
        |\n",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  Background->GrayLevel[0.95]],
 StyleBox["| scalar output f(x) in R          | P(x) - Q(x) with P, Q \
tropical polys  |\n",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  Background->GrayLevel[0.95]],
 StyleBox["| decision boundary {f = 0}        | tropical hypersurface {P = Q} \
        |\n",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  Background->GrayLevel[0.95]],
 StyleBox["| activation crease lines          | regular subdivision of Newt(P \
\\[CirclePlus] Q)        |\n",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  Background->GrayLevel[0.95]],
 StyleBox["| linear regions vs width          | Zaslavsky bound  1 + n + C(n, \
2)      |\n",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  Background->GrayLevel[0.95]],
 StyleBox["| matrix-vector  W x + b           | tropical mat-vec  A \
\\[CircleDot] x \\[CircleTimes] b           |\n",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  Background->GrayLevel[0.95]],
 StyleBox["| Bellman-Ford for shortest paths  | the SAME tropical mat-vec \
(min-plus)  |\n",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  Background->GrayLevel[0.95]],
 StyleBox["| PERT longest path                | tropical Kleene star          \
        |\n",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  Background->GrayLevel[0.95]],
 StyleBox["+----------------------------------+-------------------------------\
--------+\n",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  Background->GrayLevel[0.95]]
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bd2f0729-e41d-4cf9-ad8b-df257f5f28e0"],

Cell["\<\
Everything that ReLU networks do, max-plus algebra ALREADY does. The two are \
the same object viewed through two different operator keys.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ec4310b1-b62b-450b-9676-ca0e2a95f841"],

Cell["References", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ff91a3b5-e858-4486-8c7a-6eb171f9d2fb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Liwen Zhang, Gregory Naitzat, Lek-Heng Lim. ",
 StyleBox["Tropical Geometry of Deep Neural Networks",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". ICML 2018. arXiv:1805.07091.\n\n",
 "D. Maclagan, B. Sturmfels. ",
 StyleBox["Introduction to Tropical Geometry",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". AMS GSM 161 (2015).\n\n",
 "P. Butkovic. ",
 StyleBox["Max-linear Systems: Theory and Algorithms",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". Springer (2010).\n\n",
 "All code is at  ",
 StyleBox["github.com/mthiel74/TropicalAlgebravsReLU",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  Background->GrayLevel[0.95]],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"83d64e71-41fb-4679-8a93-40c1f781c79f"]
},
